save('process.html','How It Works','Understand the simple proposed PrintConnect print-shop workflow', '''
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Designed for busy students</span><h1>Printing should be<br>the easy part.</h1><p class="lead">A simple process, with the website handling price estimation and the proposed physical kiosk handling the actual printing.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow kicker">Our proposed workflow</span><h2>Four steps. Less hassle.</h2></div></div><div class="steps-grid"><article class="step-card"><span class="step-num">01</span><h3>Visit the website</h3><p>Open PrintConnect and check the available services and student-friendly pricing.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span class="step-num">02</span><h3>Set print details</h3><p>Use the Python calculator to select printing type and enter pages and copies.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span class="step-num">03</span><h3>Review your quote</h3><p>See the dynamic total. Generate an on-screen summary without any data upload.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span class="step-num">04</span><h3>Bring it to the kiosk</h3><p>When a campus kiosk is established, visit staff to confirm details, submit the document, and pay on-site.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section-sm"><div class="container grid-2"><div><span class="eyebrow kicker">Common questions</span><h2>Good to know<br>before you print.</h2><p class="lead" style="margin-top:20px">PrintConnect is a proposed business in our feasibility study. The prototype demonstrates how software could support students and staff.</p><a class="btn btn-dark" href="order.html" style="margin-top:24px">Estimate your cost ↗</a></div><div>
<details class="faq" open><summary>Can I actually submit an order here?</summary><p>Not yet. This is an academic prototype with a working browser-based quotation form. There is no server, payment gateway, or operational printer connected to it.</p></details>
<details class="faq"><summary>Does the site upload or save my file?</summary><p>No. If you select a local file, the browser only shows its filename. The file is never transmitted or stored by PrintConnect.</p></details>
<details class="faq"><summary>Can I print more than one copy?</summary><p>Yes. Enter a number of copies from 1 to 99, and the PyScript calculator multiplies your page count by the number of copies and price per page.</p></details>
<details class="faq"><summary>Why are scanning and photocopying not in the calculator?</summary><p>Our feasibility study does not establish final separate prices for those services. We show them as planned kiosk offerings rather than inventing unsupported charges.</p></details>
<details class="faq"><summary>Does it need a database?</summary><p>No. HTML/CSS builds the interface, while PyScript runs Python calculations and form interactions directly in the browser. Internet is needed initially to load the PyScript runtime.</p></details></div></div></section>
''')

